James asked how to use Python's `re` module to find and extract text enclosed in single or triple backticks, specifically aiming to return just the content within. I provided a solution that includes a regular expression pattern capable of matching text in both formats. The pattern allows for optional specification of "python" and captures content between backticks. I also shared a Python code snippet to demonstrate the implementation, explaining each part of the regex and its functionality to ensure clarity on how to extract the desired text effectively.
